4.2.2
Kernel density estimation
Rosenblatt [1956] proposed putting smooth Kernel weights in each of the observations. That is, around each observation Xi a Kernel function Khp  Xiq is centred. Like histogram, instead of averaging needles, one averages Kernel
functions, and we have a smoothing parameter, called the bandwidth h, regulating the degree of smoothness for Kernel
smoothers.
