4.2.4.3
The K-nearest neighbour
Deﬁnition of the K-NN estimate
Regression by Kernels is based on local averaging of observations Yi in a ﬁxed
neighbourhood around x. Rather than considering this ﬁxed neighbourhood, the K-NN employs varying neighbourhood in the X-variables which are among the K-nearest neighbours of x in Euclidean distance. Introduced by Loftsgaarden et al. [1965], it is deﬁned in the form of the general nonparametric regression estimate
