is, the shock at of a conditional Gaussian ARCHp1q model is more likely than a Gaussian white noise to produce
outliers in agreement with the empirical ﬁndings on asset returns. These properties continues to hold for general
ARCH models. Note, a natural way of achieving positiveness of the conditional variance is to rewrite an ARCHpmq
