loss. Hence, the probability that the holder would encounter a loss greater than or equal to VaR over the time horizon
d is p. Equivalently, with probability p1  pq, the potential loss encountered by the holder of the portfolio over the
time period d is less than or equal to VaR. In the case of a short position (loss when ∆V pdq ¡ 0) the Var becomes
